From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 14:41:52 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Meridian: Resume finds a project's Claude Code sessions under
 every account

Claude Code keeps its sessions per config folder. Once the owner's Work
space ran ~/.claude, Resume (Claude Code's own list) was empty there:
his 143 sessions of the project were under ~/.claude-personal.

The Workbench now asks for the project's sessions under each of the
person's Claude accounts (claudeAccountSessions: names, titles and times,
never a folder). With sessions under another account, Resume lists them
all: the space's account first, then "Earlier sessions under Personal
Claude". A session picked there runs with its own account's
CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR, its tab named after it, "Resumed with Personal
Claude" in the terminal, and it reopens under that account after a
restart. With one account, Claude Code's own list as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
